1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 12: loaded loop, toroids, L-C network and model objects

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:15,094
YA-NEC course, lesson 12: the loaded loop, toroids, the L-C network and the model objects. Calculators, Magnetic loop.

3
00:00:15,144 --> 00:00:23,094
A 1 m loop of 22 mm copper tube for 40 m: radiation resistance 6 milliohm, loss resistance 31.6 milliohm.

4
00:00:23,144 --> 00:00:30,294
So the efficiency is only 16 % (-7.9 dB). 2.45 uH tuned by 205 pF; Q 2900, bandwidth 4.9 kHz.

5
00:00:30,344 --> 00:00:38,761
And with 100 W: 52 A in the loop and 5.6 kV across the capacitor. Formulas from the ARRL Antenna Book and W5QJR.

6
00:00:38,811 --> 00:00:49,832
'Create the NEC model and check it'.

7
00:00:49,882 --> 00:00:59,966
The NEC model is fed directly in the loop, with the wires set to 'Lossless': 5.55 dBi over ground, efficiency 100 %. Too good to be true.

8
00:01:00,016 --> 00:01:09,594
Wires: Copper.

9
00:01:09,644 --> 00:01:20,061
With copper losses the gain drops to -0.13 dBi: almost 6 dB lost in the metal, as the calculator said. Always set the material on small loops.

10
00:01:20,111 --> 00:01:31,566
Now matching: the L-C network calculator.

11
00:01:31,616 --> 00:01:40,232
Load 12 - j30 ohm at 7.1 MHz onto 50 ohm: series coil 1.15 uH, shunt capacitor 798 pF; the check gives 50 + j0 ohm.

12
00:01:40,282 --> 00:01:45,293
Toroids: iron powder (T).

13
00:01:45,343 --> 00:01:52,160
Mix 2 (red), T-68 core, 2.45 uH wanted: 21 turns, 2.51 uH, mix good from 0.25 to 10 MHz.

14
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:57,230
Ferrite toroids (FT).

15
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:05,563
FT-240 in mix 43, 12 turns: 155 uH, 6.9 kohm at 7.1 MHz - a good common-mode choke. AL has a +-25 % tolerance.

16
00:02:05,613 --> 00:02:10,628
Baluns and un-uns: every ratio, with a construction drawing.

17
00:02:10,678 --> 00:02:21,161
4:1 current balun (Guanella) on two FT-240-43: 2 x 3 bifilar turns, 1 mm copper. The warning: above 30 MHz the turn capacitance makes it worse.

18
00:02:21,211 --> 00:02:28,294
Last: the model objects, under the wire table of the 3D structure tab.

19
00:02:28,344 --> 00:02:35,366
Lines: NEC TL cards, as in lessons 2 and 3.

20
00:02:35,416 --> 00:02:43,366
Transformers: an impedance ratio between two points of the model, for example the 1:6 of the Waller Flag.

21
00:02:43,416 --> 00:02:50,996
L networks and phasing networks: matching and phasing built into the model.

22
00:02:51,046 --> 00:02:59,796
And the sources: voltage or current. With 'Current sources' the program derives the voltages, as for the four-square.

23
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:05,796
Loop, toroids, L-C network, model objects: the components around the antenna. Next lesson: the other HF functions. 73 de IC8TEM
